id: triggered
name: Triggered
type: modifier
actionCost: 0
kiCost: 0
usageLimit: 1/round
baseManeuver: standard, counter, instant, outOfSequence
delays: true
asks: Select a trigger
exploitable: Any Opponent within a Sphere AoE centered on you
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Hold a Maneuver back. Pay for it now, name a trigger, and use it free and out of
  sequence if that trigger happens before your next turn starts.
text: >
  Triggered Maneuver [1/Round]: A unique type of Maneuver that allows you to delay
  your Maneuvers.
  –Action Cost: N/A
  –Base Maneuver: Any Maneuver
  –KP Cost: N/A
  –Effect: When making any type of Maneuver, you may use this Maneuver to delay its
  use but pay the Action Cost and KP Cost immediately. When you do, you must select
  a trigger. If that trigger occurs before the start of your next turn, you may use
  that Maneuver without paying the Action Cost or KP Cost as an Out-of-Sequence
  Maneuver. Below is the list of potential triggers (you may speak with your ARC to
  make any kind of trigger, but a trigger should at least be as specific as those
  below):

  * Damage: Select a Character. If that Character receives Damage, use your chosen
    Maneuver.
  * Movement: Select a Character. If that Character would use any effect to move,
    use your chosen Maneuver before they move.
  * Attack: Select a Character. If that Character uses an Attacking Maneuver, use
    your chosen Maneuver before that Attacking Maneuver is used.
  * Turn End: Select an Ally. Once that Character’s turn ends, use your chosen
    Maneuver.
  * Combat Condition: Select an Opponent and a Combat Condition. If the Opponent
    gains your selected Combat Condition, immediately use your chosen Maneuver.

  When using the Triggered Maneuver to delay a Maneuver, you provoke the Exploit
  Maneuver for any Opponent within a Sphere AoE centered on you. If you take Damage
  from an Attacking Maneuver used through the Exploit Maneuver in response to this
  Maneuver, you do not gain the effects of the Triggered Maneuver and do not use the
  selected Maneuver but you gain a number of Counter Actions equal to the Action
  Cost spent.

---

# `delays: true` is the whole of what this needed that no other Modifier has. Called
# Shot changes two numbers on the attack it was applied to; this one stops the Base
# Maneuver happening at all and hands it back later, which is a shape rather than a
# number and so has a flag.
#
# "Base Maneuver: Any Maneuver" is written as the four kinds rather than left blank,
# because a Modifier with no Base Maneuver attaches to nothing here - naming all four
# is how "any" is said.
#
# What it comes to:
#   - the Action Cost and the KP Cost are paid as the Maneuver is declared, which is
#     what the entry asks for, and then nothing else about it happens: no card, no
#     script, no Profile spent
#   - the trigger is typed in your own words and written on the card
#   - the Maneuver is held on the character and offered on that card as an
#     Out-of-Sequence Maneuver, free - the offer machinery already waives the Action
#     Cost, and `free` on the offer waives the Ki as well
#   - it lapses at the start of your next turn, which is where the entry puts it
#   - the card provokes the Exploit, because that is the Maneuver's own Exploitable
#     line written into the Effect rather than above it
#
# --- The trigger, which is the table's -------------------------------------------------
#
# "You may speak with your ARC to make any kind of trigger, but a trigger should at
# least be as specific as those below." So the five are examples of how specific to
# be, not a list to choose from, and nothing here watches for one: this system cannot
# know that a Character "would use any effect to move" before they move, and the
# entry does not ask it to. What it does is hold the Maneuver, write the trigger where
# everyone can read it, and put the button in front of the player whose Maneuver it
# is. Who says the trigger happened is the table, as it is for every range here.
#
# --- The reprisal ----------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# "If you take Damage from an Attacking Maneuver used through the Exploit Maneuver in
# response to this Maneuver, you do not gain the effects of the Triggered Maneuver and
# do not use the selected Maneuver but you gain a number of Counter Actions equal to
# the Action Cost spent."
#
# Built, and it is the first of its shape: an Exploit an offer opened carries which
# card opened it, so the Damage landing can be traced back to this one. The Ki is not
# given back - the entry hands back Counter Actions "equal to the Action Cost spent"
# and says nothing about the Ki Points, which are spent either way.
